d enabled a systemd unit (inventory-worker.service) running /usr/local/bin/os-comparison-worker as that user, verified it was active/enabled, then performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured a healthy baseline (boot_id + running service under inventorysvc), issued systemctl reboot, confirmed the node became unreachable and later reachable again with a changed boot_id, and verified inventory-worker was active, enabled, and running as inventorysvc post-restart (systemd's WantedBy=multi-user.target auto-started it, no manual intervention needed).\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected /usr/local/bin/os-comparison-worker and confirmed init system is systemd 229\",\"Created system user 'inventorysvc' via sudo useradd --system --no-create-home --shell /usr/sbin/nologin\",\"Wrote /etc/systemd/system/inventory-worker.service with User=inventorysvc, Group=inventorysvc, ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/os-comparison-worker\",\"Ran systemctl daemon-reload and systemctl enable --now inventory-worker\",\"Verified service active/enabled and main process running as inventorysvc\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline and confirmed service health\",\"Issued 'sudo systemctl reboot' on node1 in background so acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"Confirmed node1 briefly unreachable (connection refused), then polled until reachable again\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed (8336c3a1... -> 39510b7f...) proving an actual restart occurred\",\"Verified inventory-worker.service is active, enabled, and running under inventorysvc post-restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"os-comparison-worker installed as managed service 'inventory-worker' under dedicated 'inventorysvc' account\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1a129e13761a4b14\",\"cmd-83dc16e89e464524\",\"cmd-355cb0c0fb0f4037\",\"cmd-453b6a9e97c64a18\",\"cmd-2182c8afc0df44e3\"],\"summary\":\"Confirmed binary exists, created inventorysvc system user, wrote systemd unit with User=inventorysvc, enabled+started the service, and verified via ps that the running process (PID 2920) is owned by inventorysvc.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ae2eeaf4b5ec4fdd\"],\"summary\":\"Captured pre-restart boot_id (8336c3a1-91fc-4135-b26a-5d2863cb2594) as the stable boot marker, with prior command confirming service was active.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement and disconnection\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-af89c5f9de594f09\",\"cmd-e2eab139461d4d23\"],\"summary\":\"Issued 'sudo systemctl reboot' backgrounded so the exec call returned an acknowledgement before disconnect; subsequent command showed connection refused, proving the node went down.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 changed boot identity proving actual restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-006c7a7019134bd9\"],\"summary\":\"Polled until node1 became reachable again; boot_id read as 39510b7f-5faf-498a-a522-628f41f3f943, differing from the pre-restart value, and uptime -s showed a new boot time (09:15:00 vs 09:14:07).\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 post-restart service/data recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-18c58bf8f1924242\"],\"summary\":\"After restart, inventory-worker.service reported active/enabled and the running process (new PID 837) was confirmed via ps to be owned by inventorysvc, showing the service auto-started under the correct account after reboot.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"On node1, created the dedicated system account inventorysvc, installed and enabled a systemd unit (inventory-worker.service) running /usr/local/bin/os-comparison-worker as that user, verified it was active/enabled, then performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured a healthy baseline (boot_id + running service under inventorysvc), issued systemctl reboot, confirmed the node became unreachable and later reachable again with a changed boot_id, and verified inventory-worker was active, enabled, and running as inventorysvc post-restart (systemd's WantedBy=multi-user.target auto-started it, no